msgid "Keep files on disk and in the room"
msgstr ""

msgid "*See where the bytes of the study live and move them where they belong.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The files of a study live in several places at once: in the folders of "
"this computer, in the object store of a room on a StratiGraph node, "
"sometimes in a bucket that a project keeps on a server. The **Files** "
"window of the **Archive** workspace shows each of these places as one of "
"its modes, and from each mode the files can be moved where they belong. "
"The window keeps your place for each project: when you open the study "
"again, it goes back to the folder where you were."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Switch to the **Archive** workspace. The **Files** window is at the "
"centre, with the **Shelf** under it, the **Outliner** on the left and the"
" **Transformation chain (DTC)** on the right."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open a study for everything that concerns its files. With no study open, "
"the **Files** window shows **Where to start**: **Recent projects**, **+ "
"New project…** and **Allowed folders**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The **Files** window reads the disk through EMStudio's local service, the"
" bridge. If the bridge does not answer, the window says so."
msgstr ""

msgid "Walk the folders"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Files window in the mode Disk on the folder DosCo of Templu Mare: the"
" places on the left (Project, Favourites, Recent, Allowed folders), the "
"list of the files in the middle, and the tab Info on the right with the "
"gestures of this folder."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the mode menu of the **Files** window, choose **Disk**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On the left, the **Places**: **Project** (the folders of the EM standard "
"tree of the open project, see :doc:`/how-to/files/project-folder`), "
"**Favourites**, **Recent** and **Allowed folders**. A click on a place "
"opens it. **Add this folder** makes the folder you are in a favourite. "
"**The places (T)** hides and shows this column."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"At the top, the path of the folder is a breadcrumb: a click on a step "
"goes there, and ▾ chooses another folder."
msgstr ""

msgid "Desktop"
msgstr ""

msgid "▾ opens the system's folder dialog."
msgstr ""

msgid "Web"
msgstr ""

msgid "▾ opens EMStudio's own folder selector."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the folder is not among the allowed folders, EMStudio asks whether "
"to add it: only that folder becomes visible, nothing else of the disk."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To make another folder visible from the start, click **add…** under "
"**Allowed folders**. The menu lists the folders you may add; a whole disk"
" asks for confirmation first."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose **another folder…** and pick it in the system's folder dialog."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose **another folder… (type its path)** and type the absolute path of "
"the folder."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the centre, the files of the folder. **Search…** filters them by name,"
" the kind menu (**All kinds**, **Images**, **Documents**, **3D models**, "
"**Tilesets**, **em.json**, **GIS layers**) keeps one kind, and **List** "
"or **Thumbnails** changes the view. In the list, the columns **Name**, "
"**Stamp**, **In the graph**, **Size** and **Date** sort the files; a "
"second click reverses the order."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The stamps, the backup copies and the other system files are hidden. The "
"line at the bottom says how many there are, with a button such as **show "
"4 system files**; the same line counts the files, the files chosen, the "
"stamped ones and the ones to stamp."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose files with a click, more with :kbd:`⌘`-click (:kbd:`Ctrl`-click on"
" Windows and Linux), a run with :kbd:`⇧`-click. A right-click on a file "
"offers, among others, **Show in the graph**, **Put on the shelf** and "
"**Copy the path**."
msgstr ""

msgid "Work on the chosen files"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**The tools (N)** opens the panel on the right. Its four tabs work on the"
" files chosen in the centre; you can also drag the files onto a tab."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Stamp** says where a file comes from. The stamp and the chain it writes"
" are described in :doc:`/how-to/sources/declare-provenance`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Optimise** makes versions of a model for a use (see :doc:`versions-for-"
"each-use`) and packs a tileset as a ``.3tz`` (see :doc:`/how-to/space"
"/load-models-and-tilesets`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Room** uploads the files to the room you are in (see below)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Info** shows the chosen file, its stamp and its uses in the graph. With"
" no file chosen, it shows the gestures of the folder, such as the reading"
" of a DosCo folder (see :doc:`/how-to/bring-in/check-a-dosco-folder`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "See where the graph's files are"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the mode menu of the **Files** window, choose **Graph's files**. The "
"window lists the files that the active graph cites: as a list with a card"
" for each file when the window is narrow, as a table when it is wide."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click **Check the files of** followed by the name of the graph. EMStudio "
"says for each file whether it is **on this computer**, **in the room**, "
"**here and in the room**, **reference only** or **missing**, and spots an"
" **empty copy**, such as a cloud placeholder that was never downloaded."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the table, **Search files, documents, uses…** and the menus of kind "
"and use narrow the rows; a click on a row opens its card, with the "
"document that cites the file and what it is used for."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A missing file has **Find here…**, and **Find moved files…** looks for "
"all the missing files in the folders of the project. Both are described "
"in :doc:`/how-to/files/find-missing-files`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Put files in the room"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The object store of a room keeps the bytes that the room's study cites. A"
" room is entered or created as described in :doc:`/how-"
"to/rooms/create-a-room` and :doc:`/how-to/rooms/enter-and-share-a-room`; "
"the uploads also need your identity, declared in the **Identity** tab of "
"**Settings…**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the **Files** window, mode **Disk**, choose the files and open the "
"**Room** tab. It shows the licence and the embargo the files will carry, "
"and how much goes up. A file without a stamp stays private: it goes up "
"once it is stamped."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click **Upload 1 file to the room** (or **Upload** followed by the number"
" of files). The files join the room's delivery."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the mode menu, choose **In the room**. Under **The delivery — signed "
"before dragging**, check the delivery: the **Depositor** is you, taken "
"from your sign-in; write the **Author (who made it)**, or press **It was "
"me**; choose the **Licence** (the button **Use** followed by a licence "
"offers the StratiGraph default); fill **Embargo until** and **Why** when "
"the bytes must wait; give a **Name of the lot**, such as ``Flight "
"2026-03``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose **Where the bytes live**: **resident (in the room's store)** puts "
"the bytes under the node's control, so that the embargo and the licence "
"apply; **reference (they stay where they are)** records only where they "
"are, and suits material that is neither sensitive nor under embargo."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"More files can be dropped onto the area under the delivery, picked from "
"the disk, or taken from the shelf with a button such as **Take the 5 from"
" the shelf**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click **Publish** followed by the number of files. Each row says whether "
"its file is **published**, **already there** or **failed**. The bytes go "
"first, then the graph records them by their fingerprint (sha256): the "
"same bytes uploaded twice are one object."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the mode **Graph's files**, the files that are only on this computer "
"have **Upload to the room**, and the files that are only in the room have"
" **Keep on the disk too**, which copies them into the folders of the "
"project so that you can work offline."
msgstr ""

msgid "Declare a derivation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The section **Documentation (the DTC corpus)**, under the delivery, lists"
" the lots of the room. **See the DAG** draws them as acquisitions, "
"transformations and outputs; **Read the register** adds what the room's "
"server already holds about the files of the study. Under it, the form "
"**Declare a derivation** says what came out of what, with its **Output**,"
" its **Inputs** and the **Tool**; its steps are in :doc:`/how-"
"to/rooms/bring-a-file-into-a-room`. For files on the disk, the same chain"
" is written by stamping (see :doc:`/how-to/sources/declare-provenance`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Keep a copy in the bucket"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a bucket is configured for the bridge, the mode **Graph's files** "
"shows the section **Copy on the server**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click **Check** to see, for each file, whether its copy on the server "
"exists with the same size, or **Verify bytes** to compare the "
"fingerprints, which is the only proof that the two copies are the same."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On the card of a file that is only on the disk, **To the bucket** uploads"
" it, reads it back and compares it; the bucket becomes the file's main "
"address and the path on the disk stays as another address."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Once copies are verified, the button **Free the disk copy of 12 verified "
"files…** (with the number of your files) removes them from the disk. The "
"window separates the derived versions, which can be made again, from the "
"masters and originals, which are freed only if you tick them. By default "
"the files go to a ``.em_freed`` folder, from which you can take them "
"back."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To read the bucket itself, choose the mode **Bucket**: its folders and "
"files are listed as on the disk. Typing in the search field filters what "
"is listed; :kbd:`Enter` searches the names in the whole bucket under the "
"folder. Chosen files enter the study through **Bring in…** and stay in "
"the bucket, cited by their address (see :doc:`/how-to/bring-in/porta-"
"dentro`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One window that answers, for each file of the study, where its bytes are:"
" on this computer, in the room, in the bucket, or nowhere."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Files in the room with their author, licence and embargo said once for "
"the whole delivery, and derivations declared between them."
msgstr ""

msgid "Copies on the server proved identical before the disk copies are freed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The mode **Documents** of the same window shows the documents of the "
"study as a tree of their sets of files, with role, number of files, size "
"and state."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`/reference/windows`, for the **Files** window and its modes."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`the-shelf`, for the resources a study works from."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`/how-to/files/project-folder`, for the folders of an EM project."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/how-to/rooms/bring-a-file-into-a-room`, to put a whole study in a "
"room."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/reference/desktop-and-web`, for the folder dialogs of the two "
"platforms."
msgstr ""

